<DocsLayout title="batze docs — Projects" description="Organize work into projects, track time, and turn hours into invoices.">
  <h1>Projects</h1>
  <p>Group work into projects per client, track your time against them, and see what's actually worth your while.</p>

  <h2 id="time">Time tracking</h2>
  <p>Start a timer while you work, or enter hours after the fact. Each entry is attached to a project and marked billable or not.</p>

  <h2 id="rates">Rates &amp; budgets</h2>
  <p>Set a rate per project or per client, and give a project a budget so you can watch how much of it you've used as you go.</p>

  <h2 id="to-invoice">Turning time into an invoice</h2>
  <p>When you're ready to bill, batze rolls a project's billable hours into a draft <a href="/docs/invoicing">invoice</a> you can review and send.</p>
</DocsLayout>
